# Copy it to the real, gitignored file before editing:
#
#     cp .githooks/banned-identifiers.local.txt.example .githooks/banned-identifiers.local.txt
#
# Then list, one per line, the literal strings the pre-commit hook
# (.githooks/pre-commit) should refuse to let you stage: your real domain,
# your real registry hostname, your real node and cluster names, anything
# else that identifies your deployment and must never reach this public
# history. Comments start with #; blank lines are ignored.
#
# .githooks/banned-identifiers.local.txt is gitignored (see .gitignore).
# This .example file is not: it contains no real value, only the format.
